hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"250","Wa qāla sallallāhu alayhi wa sallam: Man qāla (astaghfirullāha al-adhīma alladhī lā ilāha illā huwa al-hayyu al-qayyūmu wa atūbu ilayhi), ghafarallāhu lahu wa in kāna farra min az-zahf.. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Whoever says, \I seek forgiveness from Allah"","" the Almighty"","" there is no god but He"","" the Ever-Living"","" the Self-Sustaining"","" and I repent to Him"",""\"" Allah will forgive him"","" even if he fled from the battlefield."""
"251","Wa qāla ṣallā Allāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam: Aqrabu mā yakūnu ar-Rabbu min al-ʿabdi fī jawfi al-layl al-ākhir, fa-ini istaṭaʿta an takūna mimman yadhkuru Allāh fī tilkā sāʿah fa-kun.. And he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The Lord is closest to the servant during the last part of the night; so if you can be among those who remember Allah at that hour"","" then be so.\"""
